        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(memory-wiki): salvage human Notes before pruning imported source pages",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #102230 — when `pruneImportedSourceEntries` removes a page whose syncKey\nlegitimately left `activeKeys`, it force-deletes the page file including the\nhuman-authored `## Notes` block with no salvage, archive, or tombstone.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`pruneImportedSourceEntries` calls `fs.rm` with no read of the page content\nand no check for the human Notes block. Normal syncs protect Notes via\n`preserveHumanNotesBlock`, but the prune path bypasses preservation entirely.\n\n## Fix\n\nBefore removing the page, read it and extract the human Notes block (only after\n`## Content` fence — mirrors `afterSourceContentFence` in markdown.ts). If\npresent, write to `.salvage/<page>.notes.md`. If salvage write fails, keep the\npage so Notes are not lost.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### End-to-End Proof — production function\n\n```\nnode --import tsx -e 'import { pruneImportedSourceEntries }...'\n\nBEFORE: page exists, salvage dir: no\n\nAFTER prune (1 pages): page deleted, salvage:\n<!-- openclaw:human:start -->\nreal annotations survive\n<!-- openclaw:human:end -->\nsource marker NOT salvaged: OK\n```\n\n### Regression Tests\n\n5 tests in `extensions/memory-wiki/src/source-sync-state.test.ts`:\n- salvages human Notes before pruning\n- does not create salvage files for pages without human Notes\n- prunes pages even when the page file is already missing\n- does not salvage marker comments inside source content as Notes\n- keeps the page when salvage write fails\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/memory-wiki/src/source-sync-state.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)  Tests  9 passed (9)\n```\n\n### Autoreview\n\n```\npython .agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --engine claude\nautoreview clean: no accepted/actionable findings reported\noverall: patch is correct (0.95)\n```\n\n## Change Type / Scope / Security Impact\n\n- **Change type**: `fix` — data-loss bug: prune silently destroys human Notes\n- **Scope**: memory-wiki plugin only (`extensions/memory-wiki/src/`)\n- **Security**: No new permissions, secrets, or network calls. Writes to\n  `.salvage/` under vault root with sanitized filenames. Fails-safe: if\n  salvage write fails, the page is kept.\n\n- [x] oxfmt + oxlint pass\n- [x] git diff --check pass\n- [x] autoreview clean\n",
        "branch": "fix/102230-memory-wiki-prune-notes-salvage",
